course: dictionary
lesson: 15419
title: One word, three meanings: stabbing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word stabbing has three meanings, and the words around it tell you which one. Read the whole sentence first, then ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: «The nurse said Sam had a stabbing pain in his tooth.» A stabbing pain is sudden and sharp, like something pointed pushing in. It is not a knife, because the sentence is about a pain.
explain: «Mum was stabbing a sausage with her fork to check it was cooked.» Here stabbing is a verb, the -ing form of stab. It means pushing something pointed into something.
explain: In the news, «a stabbing» is a serious crime where someone is hurt with a knife. Knives are dangerous, so never carry one, and tell a grown-up straight away if you see one.
fact: Stabbing can be a noun, an adjective or a verb form, so check the sentence to see which one it is.
fact: «A stabbing» means a crime in which someone is hurt with a knife or sharp object.
fact: «A stabbing pain» means a sudden, sharp pain.
fact: «Stabbing» as the -ing form of «stab» means pushing something pointed into something, like a fork into food.
fact: A good check is to swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «He felt a stabbing pain in his knee when he fell.» What does stabbing mean here? | *A sudden, sharp pain | A happy shout | A slow, warm feeling | A loud song
exercise: «The toddler was stabbing at her peas with a fork.» What is she doing? | Washing her plate | Counting her peas | *Pushing the pointed fork into her peas | Singing to her peas
exercise: In the news, «a stabbing» means what? | A kind surprise party | A school sports day | *A serious crime where someone is hurt with a knife | A tasty dinner
test: Which sentence uses stabbing as the -ing form of stab? | «Mia had a stabbing headache.» | «The stabbing light came on.» | «The stabbing was reported to the police.» | *«Mia was stabbing a sausage with a fork.»
test: Which phrase means a sudden, sharp pain? | a stabbing in the street | a fork | *a stabbing pain | a sharp knife
exam: What does stabbing mean in «a stabbing pain»? | A serious crime | Hiding under a bed | Pushing a fork into food | *A sudden, sharp pain
